  "notes": "Most verbs of commanding, urging and persuading (imperō, moneō, hortor, persuādeō, petō, rogō) take ut/nē + subjunctive. iubeō is the famous exception — it takes accusative + infinitive, like a verb of saying. Learn the verb WITH its construction.",
